\section{Log format}{

Each chart has one log file, \verb{<name>.jsonl}, in JSON Lines format.

The first line (header) of every logs file records \code{name}, \code{created}, the design
settings (\code{alpha}, \code{power}, \code{U0}, \code{cbar0max}, \code{amax}, \code{p_leave}, \code{n_bins}),
and the design itself (\code{delta}, \code{h}, \code{H}, \code{v}, \code{u1}). The thresholds \code{h},
\code{H} and \code{v} are rounded up to four decimals, and the chart uses these
rounded values. \code{delta} and \code{u1} are shown for completeness.

Each further line records one commit. \code{signal} is 1 if the chart ends the
commit at or above \code{h} and 0 otherwise, \code{t} is the time of the commit, \code{S}
is the CUSUM statistic at the end of the commit, rounded to four decimals,
and \code{steps} is the number of tests run.
}

